s=s.replace('Each recording consists of 30 consecutive 20-s episodes, with 10~s normal operation followed by 10~s FDIA operation.','Each recording contains 30 consecutive 20-s episodes, with 10~s normal operation followed by 10~s FDIA operation. After the scheduled 600~s, the injected bias was zero and the motor continued running. All 6,054 complete post-schedule windows are retained as normal, giving 33,054 normal and 27,000 attack windows in total.')
s=s.replace('This non-overlapping segmentation prevents temporal leakage before train/validation/test splitting.','Non-overlap prevents reuse of raw samples between adjacent windows, but does not remove within-recording dependence. Therefore, each entire recording, including its 30 episodes and post-schedule normal segment, is assigned to one partition. For each motor, five recordings are used for training, two for validation, and two for testing. Three seeds (1234, 2234, and 3234) change both the recording assignment and initialization. All feature normalization statistics are fitted using training recordings only. For example, all windows from one ACIM speed/load recording stay together; an adjacent attack episode cannot appear in a different partition. The holdouts assess new recorded operating combinations on the same apparatus; recordings can recur across repeats.')
env('fig:lfhf_motor_pcc_examples',fig('fig:lfhf_motor_pcc_examples','figure2_feature_example','Descriptive motor-current and PCC-current examples around the first scheduled attack onset in the first alphabetic held-out ACIM recording for seed 1234. LF/TD frames use 500 samples with stride 25; HF frames use 250 samples with stride 29. The vertical line marks the documented onset; feature trajectories are shown at frame centers for illustration, not as causal detector outputs. Signal amplitude is in recorded acquisition units.'),'figure')
