sub('sec:model_comparison',r'''ResNet, LSTM-FCN, Random Forest, XGBoost, and MultiRocket~\cite{tan2022multirocket} were evaluated on the same splits and corrected targets. The LSTM-FCN baseline denotes the implementation actually used, without claiming an additional squeeze-and-excitation MLSTM-FCN architecture. ResNet used 40 epochs and batch size 64; LSTM-FCN used 40 epochs, batch size 128, eight LSTM units, dropout 0.5, and convolutional widths 64/128/64. Trees used the flattened $61\times F$ tensors: Random Forest compared 300/600 trees and unrestricted/20 depth with balanced-subsample weights; XGBoost compared depth 4 with learning rate 0.05 and depth 6 with learning rate 0.03, using 1,500 estimators and 0.8 row/column subsampling. MultiRocket used approximately 50,000 transformed features and ridge penalties 0.1/1/10/100. Available candidate settings were selected using validation balanced accuracy. Search budgets differ between model families, so this is a comparison under the stated settings rather than an equal-budget optimization study.

As shown in Table~\ref{tab:model_comparison_hard_tasks}, InceptionTime has the highest mean PCC balanced accuracy for both tasks, and the highest mean accuracy and macro F1 for binary detection. For severity, XGBoost has higher raw accuracy (70.45\% versus 61.00\%), while LSTM-FCN has slightly higher macro F1 (53.23\% versus 52.96\%). InceptionTime's severity advantage is confined to mean balanced accuracy (55.62\% versus at most 52.38\% among the evaluated alternatives). Unequal class counts make these distinctions material; no statistical-significance claim is made from three overlapping repeated holdouts.

'''+basetable)
